{#
  partials/tile.njk — THE tile. One person-shaped thing in a .profile-grid.

  Usage: set `tile` before including.
    {% set tile = { href: "/profiles/kim-il/", photo: "/assets/img/…", name: "Kim Il" } %}
    {% include "partials/tile.njk" %}

  Fields, all optional except href and name:
    href   where the whole tile links
    photo  image path; without one the tile shows the `empty` label instead
    empty  what to say in place of a missing photograph (default "No photograph")
    name   the line under the picture
    sub    a second line under the name, quieter — a Korean name, a handle
    lang   the language of `sub`, for screen readers (default "ko")
    badge  a short status word rendered as a .badge--high chip beside the name
    attrs  extra attributes for the <li>, as a raw string (search hooks)

  There is one tile design on this site and this is it: the named IT workers,
  the personas, and the profiles a cluster page previews all render through
  here. Before adding a card class, check whether this covers it — a second
  tile that is nearly the same is how a site stops looking like one site.

  DELIBERATELY ON ONE LINE, and it must stay that way. src/index.md includes
  this through Nunjucks and then Markdown, and markdown-it treats a raw HTML
  block containing blank lines as markdown: it wraps the pieces in <p> tags,
  which inside an <a> is invalid markup the browser repairs by splitting the
  anchor in two, rendering every tile twice. If you reformat this for
  readability, check the home page still renders one tile per profile.
#}
<li{% if tile.attrs %} {{ tile.attrs | safe }}{% endif %}><a class="profile-card" href="{{ tile.href }}">{% if tile.photo %}<img class="profile-card__photo" src="{{ tile.photo }}" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">{% else %}<span class="profile-card__photo profile-card__photo--empty">{{ tile.empty | default("No photograph") }}</span>{% endif %}<span class="profile-card__name">{{ tile.name }}{% if tile.badge %} <span class="badge badge--high">{{ tile.badge }}</span>{% endif %}{% if tile.sub %}<span class="profile-card__name-ko" lang="{{ tile.lang | default("ko") }}">{{ tile.sub }}</span>{% endif %}</span></a></li>
